WEBVTT


00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.140
This Valentine's pillow is shaped
as it's knit on the machine.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.510
No cut 'n sew for this project, there are
two methods you can use to create your

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.890
knitting instructions for your gauge.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:23.780
Use DesignaKnit and create your shape or
draw a template and work out the shaping

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.010
it with paper and pencil.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.540
Tutorials for both of these
methods are available.

00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:35.355
This video will focus on the
knitting and shaping of this pillow.

00:00:37.195 --> 00:00:42.025
Take a look at the drawing for my pillow
at my gauge, and you'll notice that I need

00:00:42.025 --> 00:00:44.245
to start with one stitch.

00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:49.545
I don't know about you, but starting with
a single stitch and increasing to create a

00:00:49.545 --> 00:00:52.425
V shape isn't one of my
favorite things to do.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:54.225
Here's a better way.

00:00:54.405 --> 00:00:55.605
Use short rows.

00:00:56.665 --> 00:01:03.695
The widest point of my heart is 104
stitches all cast on those 104 stitches

00:01:03.695 --> 00:01:05.495
with waste yarn and ravel cord.

00:01:12.635 --> 00:01:16.685
Next, I'll e-wrap across all of
the needles with the main yarn.

00:01:23.985 --> 00:01:28.095
After I finished the initial e-wrap, I
broke the yarn and removed it from the

00:01:28.095 --> 00:01:28.845
carriage.

00:01:29.294 --> 00:01:33.405
I'm going to start with a new end
of yarn in the center of the bed.

00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:39.994
Now to make things a little easier, I
e-wrap cast on two stitches and then hand

00:01:39.994 --> 00:01:43.145
knit those two stitches
through the original cast on.

00:01:45.295 --> 00:01:51.125
You notice, I'll position my working yarn
over the needles in hold and I'll thread

00:01:51.145 --> 00:01:52.135
up the carriage.

00:01:54.705 --> 00:01:59.955
Then I've set my carriage to hold position
and I'll start knitting from the center of

00:01:59.955 --> 00:02:00.615
the bed.

00:02:01.865 --> 00:02:06.245
With each row knit, I'll follow my
pattern, putting needles in work to

00:02:06.245 --> 00:02:08.735
increase and form the V shape.

00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:14.195
Notice that you'll need some weight in the
center as you knit to keep those stitches

00:02:14.195 --> 00:02:15.365
from popping off

00:02:17.995 --> 00:02:21.655
because this edge will be enclosed
in a seam to create my pillow,

00:02:21.655 --> 00:02:25.915
I'm not worrying about wrapping stitches
as you normally would with short rows.

00:02:27.445 --> 00:02:31.705
I'll keep following my chart until all
of the stitches are in working position.

00:02:32.395 --> 00:02:36.715
Then I'll turn off the hold setting and
at the straight section of my design.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:43.100
When I get to the shaping for the top of
the heart, I'm going to split the row and

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.900
shape one side at a time.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.710
You could remove half of the stitches on
waste yarn, but because this section is

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.310
fairly short, I'm just going to hang a bit
of waste knitting on the needles in hold.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:01.800
This will protect the knitting from
the carriage as I work the other side.

00:03:08.059 --> 00:03:10.130
Working on the right side of my heart.

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:14.630
I'll keep those left stitches inhold
position and set the carriage to hold.

00:03:16.649 --> 00:03:22.880
Then again, following the diagram, I'll
decrease on both sides as I knit forming

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:29.459
that curved shape to make seaming easier,
I like to work my decreases one or two

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:30.989
stitches in from the edge.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.239
Continue the shaping
according to your pattern.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.839
Bind off the last row
and you're halfway there.

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:48.820
Remove the protective swatch and shape the
left side of the knitting to mirror the

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:49.329
right.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:53.720
Voila.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.149
A beautiful heart shape.

00:03:57.529 --> 00:03:59.750
Knit a second one to finish up.

00:04:01.955 --> 00:04:07.205
When you remove the waste yarnamfrom the
bottom edge, it'll be beautiful and easy

00:04:07.205 --> 00:04:07.685
to see.

00:04:09.085 --> 00:04:13.705
In the next video, we'll seam,
stuff and embellish the pillow

